\title{a5pyramid: Level-of-Detail Pyramids of A5 Cells for Browser Rendering}
\description{
a5pyramid builds level-of-detail pyramids of \href{https://a5geo.org/}{A5}
cells, as created by \link[a5R:a5R-package]{a5R} and a5px, and writes them
with the cells they summarise to one Parquet file laid out for browsers.
A web map reads the file's footer, picks the level for its zoom, and
fetches only the tiles in view with HTTP range requests, for example
with hyparquet and deck.gl. The engine is a Rust crate with no R
dependency, built to be published on its own.
}
\section{Building}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=a5_pyramid]{a5_pyramid()}}: build the levels in memory and return them as a tibble.
\item \code{\link[=a5_write_pyramid]{a5_write_pyramid()}}: build the levels and write them to Parquet, in
Rust from end to end.
\item \code{\link[=a5_pyramid_arrow]{a5_pyramid_arrow()}}: build the levels and return the tiles of the
Parquet layout in memory, as an Arrow table, without a file.
}

Each coarser level groups the leaves by the coarse cell containing their
centres (\code{\link[a5R:a5_cell_to_supercell]{a5R::a5_cell_to_supercell()}}) and reduces each column by mean,
sum, minimum, maximum, mode or a representative leaf.
}

\section{Reading}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=a5_pyramid_info]{a5_pyramid_info()}}: the file's index and layout, from its footer.
\item \code{\link[=a5_read_pyramid]{a5_read_pyramid()}}: the rows of chosen levels within a bounding box,
read as a renderer reads them.
}
}

\section{Threads}{

\code{\link[=a5pyramid_threads]{a5pyramid_threads()}} sets how many threads builds use; the default is
every available CPU. Builds can be interrupted (Ctrl-C, or Esc in an
IDE).
}

\section{Errors}{

Errors raised by a5pyramid have class \code{a5pyramid_error} and one of:
\itemize{
\item \code{a5pyramid_error_input}: invalid arguments or cells, such as cells at
mixed resolutions or a duplicated cell.
\item \code{a5pyramid_error_io}: a file or directory that cannot be read or
written.
\item \code{a5pyramid_error_format}: a file that is not a pyramid, or one written
for another A5 index or a newer format version.
\item \code{a5pyramid_error_interrupted}: a build stopped by the user.
\item \code{a5pyramid_error_internal}: a fault in a5pyramid; please report it.
}
